s description beside each code. It does not count projects: one project can contain PINs in several classes. Because the sample includes properties that were commercial or industrial in earlier years, residential, vacant, and exempt classes can also appear. The final missing-record category has no known 2024 classification.\n\n\n::: {#tbl-class-summary .cell tbl-cap='PIN counts by 2024 property class'}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|2024 class |Description                   | PINs|\n|:----------|:-----------------------------|----:|\n|517        |One-story commercial building |    1|\n|535        |Golf course improvement       |    2|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Projects in Golf\n\nCounts and values include only PINs within this region. A project may extend into another region, so regional project counts are not additive. Unassigned PINs are excluded from project totals. FMV means estimated fair market value. Incentive PINs are 2024 classes 600-899. FMV is summed only over known 2024 values; an entirely missing valuation remains missing. The project identifier uses Appellant, falling back to Key PIN. Last Year of Paid Taxbill lists each distinct latest year in which a PIN had a bill greater than $0 during 2006-2024; it does not confirm payment. PINs without a positive bill in that history are identified separately. TIF counts use 2024 PIN-to-TIF membership records regardless of payment or increment, rather than positive distributions. Missing 2024 records are not counted as known TIF members.\n\n\n::: {#tbl-projects .cell .column-screen-inset tbl-cap='Projects, appellants, and 2024 values'}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-55540c9a215281b5b1f8\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;\" class=\"datatables html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-55540c9a215281b5b1f8\">{\"x\":{\"filter\":\"top\",\"vertical\":false,\"filterHTML\":\"<tr>\\n  <td data-type=\\\"character\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: top;\\\">\\n  